<p>Contacts don't fail because of astigmatism, keratoconus, or dry eye. They fail because most fittings never dig deep enough to account for those conditions in the first place. Hard-to-fit contact lenses in Forest Hills exist for exactly this reason, and the right fit usually depends less on the eye and more on who is doing the fitting.</p>
<p>At Austin Optics, that person is Mark Kimyagarov, a licensed <a href="{{ route('meet-the-team') }}">optician</a> who has spent over 15 years working through cases that other practices pass on. This guide walks through what actually makes an eye hard to fit, what the process looks like when it is done properly, and why patients who gave up on contacts years ago sometimes end up wearing them comfortably again.</p>

